Design rules (must follow):
Color rules:
- Only two functional hues: emerald (#10B981 header/fills, #059669 buttons/text,
  #D1FAE5 tint) and risk red (#D64560).
- Everything else is neutral: #F5F5F5, #FFFFFF, #E5E7EB, #9CA3AF, #6B7280, #1F2937.
- No amber, blue, purple, or orange in the UI. The only exception is the 3px
  vertical course lines on timetable rows: #2563EB, #EA580C, #DB2777.
- No pure black (#000) anywhere.
- No navbar, tab bar, drawer, or floating action buttons.
- Rows are flat: white, 1px #E5E7EB border, 6px radius, no shadow, 12px padding.
- Spacing only from 4/8/12/16/24/32. Font sizes only 12/14/16/20/28. Weights 400/500/600.
- Max 3 screens: Today, Attendance, Simulator. Alerts are a popover.
- Do not add features, screens, or controls that were not requested.

Assignment exceptions (allowed and required):
- The Attendance screen has an "Add course" modal form (a modal, not a screen).
  Entry point is a text button in the "Your courses" heading row, never a floating button.
- The Attendance screen shows two react-native-chart-kit charts (LineChart, BarChart)
  below the course rows. Charts must render on the phone layout, not only on wide screens.
- Chart and form styling must still follow the color and spacing rules above.

After every Cursor run, open the search (Ctrl+Shift+F) and look for leftovers: blue, #2563, shadow, rounded-2xl, fixed bottom. If they show up, tell Cursor to remove them.
